  {
   "id": "eng.vocab.context-clues",
   "name": "Guessing meaning from context",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "You can guess a new word's meaning from the sentence around it. \"The New Year commenced in Spring, on March 1\" tells you commenced means began. \"Tiu's Day gradually evolved into Tuesday\" shows evolve means change gradually. A version is a slightly different form; placement is position; tracing means following something back to its origin."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "የአዲስ ቃልን ትርጉም ከዙሪያው ዓረፍተ ነገር መገመት ትችላለህ፤ \"commenced\" = ጀመረ፣ \"evolved\" = ቀስ በቀስ ተለወጠ።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
